  "summary": "Serve one embedding model in two configurations, one tuned for single-query latency and one for bulk backfill throughput, and test whether an 8-bit copy of the model keeps cosine similarity at 0.99 or better and returns the same nearest neighbours. Runs on a laptop CPU; a GPU is optional.",
  "deliverables": [
    "A lookup path: one text per request at a fixed request rate, with latency at P50 and P95 over at least 200 requests.",
    "A backfill path: at least 10,000 documents embedded at three or more batch sizes, with documents per second and peak memory for each.",
    "An 8-bit copy of the model (for example ONNX Runtime dynamic INT8, or FP8 on a GPU) compared with the original on at least 1,000 inputs: mean, minimum and P5 cosine similarity.",
    "A retrieval check: overlap of the top 10 neighbours from both models for at least 100 queries.",
    "charts/backfill-throughput.png: documents per second against batch size.",
    "A Makefile whose check target runs both paths and the quality check with --dry-run, using a tiny stand-in model, and writes only under $OUT_DIR."
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "Pick a model of 1B parameters or fewer and name it with its output dimensions.",
    "Use one public text dataset for both paths and name it.",
    "State the hardware, thread count and runtime version.",
    "make check finishes in under 8 minutes on 2 CPUs with no network and a read-only repo."
  ],
  "skills": ["Embedding inference", "Batching", "Quantization quality checks", "Throughput tuning"],
